## Reading

The two rounds waited 397 s and 401 s, a difference of 4 s (1%). Both ran on the same node in the default `batch` partition.
These are two observations about 10 minutes apart on one shared cluster, under queue load that was not controlled or recorded.
They show that a 1-CPU, 2-minute job waited about 6.6 minutes both times on this morning (UTC). They do not give a typical or
worst-case wait, a distribution, or a trend. Round 2 differed from round 1 in being measured from an idle repository, but with one job per round the 4 s gap cannot be attributed to that or to anything else.

